<title>USA: Blue-chip stocks slash losses.</title>
<headline>Blue-chip stocks slash losses.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK</dateline>
<text>
<p>Blue-chip stocks staged a late recovery from deep losses Wednesday as bargain-hunters and strength in Philip Morris Cos. came to the market's rescue.</p>
<p>Based on early and unofficial data, the Dow Jones industrial average ended down 19.75 points at 6,422.94 after shaking off a huge loss of more than 75 points. In the broader market, declining issues led advances 14-10 on active volume of 498 million shares on the New York Stock Exchange.</p>
